- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests`

**How to implement.** The column-mapping wizard also opens on a file to split across the kit's experiments, so the data dialog's preview, column roles and profile picker serve the split too (001 §O 'Data dialog: preview, column roles, an import-profile picker, the key split with a matched / unmatched table'; the S9.3 brief: the profile picker (S9.2); .spec-md §6 'Reuse before invention': one wizard). The Data step's button that opens it is step 323's. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportWizardView.fs` (step 308): before `ImportWizardRequest`, `ImportWizardTarget` = `AttachWizardTarget of Experiments.ExperimentId` (attach the file to that experiment) | `SplitWizardTarget` (split the file across the kit's experiments by its key column), each case documented in one line. `ImportWizardRequest` and `ImportWizardApplied` replace `experimentId` with `target : ImportWizardTarget`, and `ApplyImportWizard` hands the request's target on unchanged; nothing else in the model or the update changes. `importWizardView` (step 309) reads the target in two places only: the heading is `Import <the file's leaf name>` for `AttachWizardTarget` and `Split <the file's leaf name> by its key column` for `SplitWizardTarget`, and `importWizardAttachButton` is captioned `Attach` or `Split`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `ImportWizardApplied.messages` (step 310) answers, after `SaveImportProfile p` when `savedOpt` is `Some p`, `AttachDataFile (id, file, profile)` for `AttachWizardTarget id` and `SplitByColumn (file, profile)` (step 319) for `SplitWizardTarget`, so a new profile is in the kit before a file is mapped or split by it. `OpenImportWizard` (step 310) builds its request with `target = AttachWizardTarget experimentId`. New `OpenSplitWizard of FileName` (the Data step's Split a file by key… after its file dialog), documented in one line and refused by the read-only guard of step 185: it calls `model.kitShell.openImportWizard { target = SplitWizardTarget; file; readPickedFile = model.experimentData.readPickedFile; kitProfiles = model.kit.kitFile.importProfiles; defaultProfile = ImportProfileName.phoneRoiCsv }` (the built-in that carries a key column, step 298) and answers the model unchanged. `ImportWizardWindow` and `withImportWizard` (step 311) are unchanged: the shell opens one wizard for either target. No other message, field or option is added. Tests. `ImportWizardTests` (steps 308, 309, 311): the class's request takes `target = AttachWizardTarget (ExperimentId 1)`; `Attach with a picked profile hands it to the kit window once and closes` and `Attach with a new mapping hands the kit window the profile to save and attaches by it` record an `onApplied` whose `target` is `AttachWizardTarget (ExperimentId 1)`, their other assertions kept; every other fact passes with that request; new `a split wizard says it splits and hands the kit window the file and the profile to split by`: over the class's request with `target = SplitWizardTarget`, `importWizardView` mounted as the class mounts it shows the heading `Split <leaf> by its key column` and the button `Split`, and `PickImportProfile` of `Phone ROI CSV` then `ApplyImportWizard` record one `onApplied` of `SplitWizardTarget`, the file, `Phone ROI CSV` and `None`, then one close. `KitWindowModelTests` (step 310): `opening the import wizard hands it the picked file, the kit's profiles and the detector's default` records a request whose `target` is `AttachWizardTarget (ExperimentId 1)`; `the wizard's Attach saves its new mapping first and attaches the file by it` builds its applied value with that target, its assertions kept; new `opening the split wizard hands it the picked file with Phone ROI CSV chosen, and its Apply splits by the chosen profile`: `OpenSplitWizard <a test-local file>` records one request of `SplitWizardTarget`, that file, the kit's profiles and `defaultProfile` `Phone ROI CSV`, the model unchanged; `messages` of an applied `{ SplitWizardTarget; <the file>; Lab scan; Some <step 310's test-local Lab scan> }` are `[ SaveImportProfile <it>; SplitByColumn (<the file>, Lab scan) ]`. `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` also sends `OpenSplitWizard`, recording no request. `ScrollExtentTests`' `the import wizard leaves everything reachable` (step 311) builds its request with `target = AttachWizardTarget (ExperimentId 1)`, its assertions kept.

**Acceptance.** After the wizard gains its target, the same wizard MUST open on a file to attach to one experiment or to split across the kit's experiments, say which, and hand the kit window `AttachDataFile` or `SplitByColumn` after any new profile is saved, and `OpenSplitWizard` MUST open it with Phone ROI CSV chosen, refused under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `opening the split wizard hands it the picked file with Phone ROI CSV chosen, and its Apply splits by the chosen profile`, the count rising by 1, and the changed `opening the import wizard hands it the picked file, the kit's profiles and the detector's default`, `the wizard's Attach saves its new mapping first and attaches the file by it` and `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a split wizard says it splits and hands the kit window the file and the profile to split by`, the count rising by 1, and the changed `Attach with a picked profile hands it to the kit window once and closes` and `Attach with a new mapping hands the kit window the profile to save and attaches by it`; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.
